@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;protocol] illumos-host-only-socket-boundary
The illumos socket module MUST require global-zone system-configuration privilege,
use public AF_VSOCK 40 and the reviewed 16-byte address, and accept only incoming
host CID 2 streams on guest CID 3. Payload and socket allocations MUST remain
bounded. Guest-initiated streams and unused socket options MUST be refused.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] illumos-transport-lifetime
Transport reset or configuration change MUST fence existing sockets, including
listeners and unbound sockets. A fenced socket MUST NOT bind or listen again.
Callback unsubscription MUST prevent replacement until existing callbacks drain;
queue DMA MUST outlive interrupt and worker drainage. Syscall copies MUST hold
references, preserve exclusive buffer ownership, and revalidate credit/shutdown
before publishing bytes copied without the socket lock.
An activated transport MUST NOT reclaim queues, interrupts or DMA without a
proven backend reset. The static driver MUST refuse runtime detach and retain an
unavailable attachment after any post-activation failure until VM disposal.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity;recovery] illumos-block-request-budget
Without negotiated indirect descriptors, the block driver MUST bound concurrent
requests by each request's maximum data segments plus its header and status
descriptors. Data DMA scatter limits MUST fit the direct ring; a ring unable to
hold one request MUST refuse attachment. Indirect request depth MUST remain
bounded by the ring and the fixed request pool.
Completion MUST return the request and its descriptors before notifying blkdev,
which can synchronously submit a new DMA window or queued request. The original
completion error MUST survive immediate request reuse, and the completed request
MUST NOT be touched after the callback begins.
Completed blkdev transfers MUST return submission success after notifying the
framework exactly once, including polled errors. Internal transfers without a
blkdev callback MUST return their original completion error directly.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] illumos-module-evidence-boundary
Cross-compiled ELF objects MUST NOT be described as native linked kernel modules,
a bootable kernel or image admission. Module integration requires the matching
modern virtio framework and all five consumer drivers, the opt-in sockfs listener
failure changes, a native Solaris kernel-module link and native machine evidence.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;verification] illumos-kernel-syscall-symbols
The cross build MUST undefine userland feature-test macros that rename kernel
sockfs syscall definitions. Actual socksyscalls.o exports MUST include ordinary
bind, connect, getsockopt, recvmsg, sendmsg and sendto, and MUST NOT define renamed
__xnet_* symbols. Native linkage MUST require the corresponding verified receipt.
